#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=9 nAlgorithms=6;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version dev) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1792653203197'; [Thu Oct 22 09:13:23 CEST 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[!
Phylogenetic analysis of the Huon Peninsula languages.
Citation: SJ Greenhill, TransNewGuinea.org: An Online Database of New Guinea Languages, PLoSOne 2015,
https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0141563
Originally sourced from:
McElhanon, K.A. 1967. Preliminary Observations on Huon Peninsula Languages. Oceanic Linguistics. 6, 1-45.
Alignment of 14 languages is based on 391 cognate sets.]

[
Input:
Phylogenetic analysis of the Huon Peninsula languages.
Citation: SJ Greenhill, TransNewGuinea.org: An Online Database of New Guinea Languages, PLoSOne 2015,
https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0141563
Originally sourced from:
McElhanon, K.A. 1967. Preliminary Observations on Huon Peninsula Languages. Oceanic Linguistics. 6, 1-45.
Alignment of 14 languages is based on 391 cognate sets.

Methods:
Analysis was performed using SplitsTree (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.).
The original input consisted of 14 taxa and 14 Standard sequences of length 391.
The Hamming Distance method (Hamming 1950) was used (default options) so as to obtain a 14 x 14 distance matrix.
The Neighbor Net method (Bryant & Moulton 2004, Bryant & Huson 2023) was used (default options) so as to obtain 45 splits, circular.
The Show Splits method was used (default options) so as to obtain a Split Network visualization.

References:
Bryant & Huson 2023: D. Bryant and DH Huson, NeighborNet- improved algorithms and implementation. Front. Bioinform. 3, 2023.
Bryant & Moulton 2004: D. Bryant and V. Moulton. Neighbor-net: An agglomerative method for the construction of phylogenetic networks. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 21(2):255– 265, 2004.
Hamming 1950: Hamming, Richard W. Error detecting and error correcting codes. Bell System Technical Journal. 29 (2): 147-160. MR 0035935, 1950.
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

